# Frontend rules

## Stack

Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, Axios via **`lib/axios.ts`** (`withCredentials: true`).

## Layering (do not invert)

| Layer | Path | Role |
|-------|------|------|
| Routes | `app/**/page.tsx` | Thin shells — auth, layout, compose one feature view |
| Features | `features/<domain>/**` | Screens, hooks, local types |
| Shared UI | `components/ui/**` | Primitives — reuse before duplicating |
| API | `lib/*Api.ts` | All backend HTTP calls |

- **No raw HTTP in `app/`** for app APIs.
- **`lib/` must not import `features/`.**
- **Tailwind** for all styling; brand tokens in **`globals.css`**.

## Thin pages

Route files: auth/shell + one feature view. Extract to **`features/<domain>/*View.tsx`** + hook when a page grows past ~50 lines of state/effects.

## Mutations

Use **`useToast()`** + **`lib/mutationFeedback.ts`** for save/send/approve feedback. Chat send is implicitly OK (no toast).

## Conventions

- API paths only in **`lib/*Api.ts`** — match `/api/v1/...`.
- Forms: Zod via **`lib/validation/`**.
- Buttons: **`components/ui/Button.tsx`**; loading: **`LoadingState`** / **`LoadingSpinner`**.
- Back nav: **`BackLink.tsx`**.
- **Sentry:** `NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN` empty = no-op. Shared options in `lib/sentryConfig.ts` (`getSentrySharedInitOptions`); the three Next entrypoints only call `Sentry.init` with those options (Replay stays client-only). Do not drop `next.config.ts` rewrites when wrapping `withSentryConfig`.

Details: **`docs/architecture-reference.md`** (Frontend section).
